  "reproduction_script": "import hashlib,json,sys,random,math\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom fractions import Fraction as F\nfrom itertools import product\nROOT=Path('/home/lunarz/worktrees/roboboat-terminal-evidence');sys.path.insert(0,str(ROOT/'analysis'))\nimport roboboat_fixed_n_interval_exact_v1 as ex\npaths=['analysis/roboboat_fixed_n_interval_exact_v1.py','tests/test_roboboat_fixed_n_interval_exact_v1.py','docs/roboboat_terminal_evidence/FIXED_N_EXACT_INTERVAL_CANDIDATE_V1.md']\nbindings=[{'path':p,'sha256':hashlib.sha256((ROOT/p).read_bytes()).hexdigest()} for p in paths]\nlam,w,alpha=ex.settings(['1/4','1/2','3/4'],[1,2,1],'1/40')\n# Independent direct product implementation: no Counter or candidate e_value.\ndef direct(values,m):\n return sum(weight*math.prod(1-bet+bet*(F(v,6)+1)/(1+m) for v in values) for bet,weight in zip(lam,w))\nrng=random.Random(91300);panels=[[-6]*3,[6]*3,[-6,6],[-5,-3,0,1,6]]\npanels += [[rng.randint(-6,6) for _ in range(rng.randint(1,25))] for _ in range(24)]\nchecks=[]\nfor values in panels:\n lo,hi=ex.lower_bracket(values,lam,w)\n if all(v==-6 for v in values):assert lo==hi==-1\n else:\n  assert hi-lo==F(2,2**48)\n  assert lo==-1 or direct(values,lo)*alpha>=1\n  assert direct(values,hi)*alpha<1\n  assert F.from_float(ex.outward_float(lo,-1))<=lo\n  assert F.from_float(ex.outward_float(hi,1))>=hi\n adverse=[max(-6,v-rng.randint(0,3)) for v in values]\n favorable=[min(6,v+rng.randint(0,3)) for v in values]\n complete=ex.interval(values,values,lam,w);missing=ex.interval(adverse,favorable,lam,w)\n assert F(missing['exact_outer_bounds'][0])<=F(complete['exact_outer_bounds'][0])\n assert F(missing['exact_outer_bounds'][1])>=F(complete['exact_outer_bounds'][1])\n checks.append({'values':values,'outer_bounds':complete['exact_outer_bounds'],'adverse':adverse,'favorable':favorable,'missing_bounds':missing['exact_outer_bounds']})\n# Exact enumerations of weak average null with deliberately unequal means.\nenumerations=[]\nfor ps in [[F(1,8),F(3,8),F(5,8),F(7,8)],[F(0),F(0),F(1),F(1)],[F(1,10),F(2,10),F(3,10),F(4,10)]]:\n evmean=F(0);reject=F(0)\n for bits in product([0,1],repeat=len(ps)):\n  prob=math.prod(p if b else 1-p for p,b in zip(ps,bits));values=[6 if b else -6 for b in bits]\n  e=direct(values,F(0));evmean+=prob*e\n  if e*alpha>=1:reject+=prob\n assert evmean<=1 and reject<=alpha\n enumerations.append({'probabilities':list(map(str,ps)),'average_mean':str(sum(2*p-1 for p in ps)/len(ps)),'exact_expected_e':str(evmean),'exact_rejection_probability':str(reject)})\nreport={'schema':'roboboat-exact-interval-independent-review/v1','origin':'SIMULATED','sources':bindings,\n'proof_review':{'fixed_N_weak_average_null':'For independent bounded D_i and fixed m>-1, each positive factor has expectation a_i=1-lambda+lambda*(mu_i+1)/(1+m)>0. Independence gives product a_i; arithmetic mean a_i<=1 under average mu_i<=m, hence AM-GM gives expectation<=1. Fixed normalized mixture preserves the bound; Markov gives each tail alpha. The target is the arithmetic mean of independent per-geometry expectations at the fixed allocation, not an unqualified superpopulation or per-geometry effect.',\n'inversion':'Factors decrease in m, strictly for at least one D_i>-1; other factors remain positive constants. Exact rational threshold comparisons preserve the outer bracket; lower outer endpoint is conservative even at threshold atoms. All-minus-one lower endpoint is support bound. Negation gives upper endpoint, and union bound gives coverage at least 1-2*alpha.',\n'missingness':'Pointwise score bounds plus endpoint monotonicity give realization-wise containment regardless of outcome-dependent missingness, provided the full fixed-N identities remain represented. Dropping missing identities would invalidate this reasoning.',\n'float_conversion':'Exact Fraction.from_float comparison and one outward nextafter correctly conservatively round these finite rational endpoints in [-1,1].'},\n'independent_hypothetical_panels':checks,'